 "Tomáš Macháč"] ", the eventual gold medalists. It was Czechia’s first Olympic mixed doubles medal, and Siniaková’s second Olympic gold, after winning the women’s doubles in 2021. A doubles specialist, Siniaková had won nine Grand Slam trophies prior to the Paris Olympics."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the bronze medal match, Canada’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/129518"} "Gaby Dabrowski"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/141561"} "Félix Auger-Aliassime"] " defeated " [:a {:href "/athletes/145519"} "Demi Schuurs"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/145600"} "Wesley Koolhof"] " of the Netherlands. It was Canada’s second Olympic medal in this event. About four months after the 2024 Paris Olympics, Dabrowski revealed that she had breast cancer. She also revealed that she had been diagnosed prior to the Olympics but delayed chemotherapy treatment of the breast cancer to enable her to play in Paris."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/142069"} "Kateřina Siniaková"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/142116"} "Tomáš Macháč"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CZE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CZE.png"}] "CZE"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/2504729"} "Wang Xinyu"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/154910"} "Zhang Zhizhen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/129518"} "Gaby Dabrowski"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/141561"} "Félix Auger-Aliassime"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "